<title>UK: ED&amp;F Man Investment ties up with Bank of NZ.</title>
<headline>ED&amp;F Man Investment ties up with Bank of NZ.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>ED&amp;F Man Investment Products said on Wednesday it and the Bank of New Zealand were developing the first futures-backed investment notes to be offered in the New Zealand market.</p>
<p>The BNZ Capital Guaranteed Growth Notes, to be offered between Feburary 18 and April 4, mature in 2007 and carry an annual variable coupon.</p>
<p>The issue size is capped at NZ$20 million with a minimum investment of NZ$5,000.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7770 (fax +44 171 583 7239)</p>
</text>
